# Every file checks out in its committed form, because plan 5.3 requires a
# ticket file to carry LF line endings and git converts to CRLF on Windows by
# default. Without this line a Windows checkout rewrites every fixture, and
# parse then refuses the file it just read: "file does not start with a ---
# frontmatter fence". The Windows lane went red on exactly that, on the push
# that added it, over 30 fixtures at once.
#
# This protects a checkout of this repository. It does nothing for a user's own
# repository, whose .tickets/ has no such line unless somebody wrote one.
* text=auto eol=lf

.tickets/**/*.md merge=gitticket
